Restart can persist stale PG observations and brick state
Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/security/findings/6092396d3b588191ac3502c526c8cda4?sev=&repo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fjustincormack%2Fargmin
Criticality: informational (attack path: ignore)
Status: fixed

# Resolution
Fixed in commit `45993585 Clear PG observations on authority restart`.

The finding was valid as a Phase 11 control-plane reliability defect. The
restart epoch-bump path now clears current PG observations, matching ordinary
epoch-change behavior, while preserving the pre-restart observations in
cluster-map history for diagnostics. The fix includes a regression test that
plants a valid current-epoch PG observation, restarts once, verifies the current
map no longer persists stale observations, and then restarts again successfully.

